vaporOS NuttX patch: vfs-stat-zero-mountpoint

Problem:   `ls -l /bin` (any mounted filesystem that fills only part of struct
           stat) printed garbage: owner 3735928559 (0xDEADBEEF), link count
           48879 (0xBEEF), dates like "12847078-50427214-49 53:235", and a
           "total 1.7G". Seen on the RP2040 and on the simulator.
Evidence:  nx_stat() zeroes the buffer (RESET_BUF) for pseudo-filesystem nodes
           but not before calling a mountpoint's stat(). binfs_stat() sets only
           st_mode, st_size, st_blksize and st_blocks (st_uid/gid only with
           SCHED_USER_IDENTITY), so every other field is leftover stack/heap
           content. The pasted values are the heap-poison pattern 0xDEADBEEF.
Fix:       RESET_BUF(buf) before dispatching to the mountpoint's stat().
           A single line that protects every filesystem, present and future,
           rather than patching binfs alone.
Upstream:  YES. A plain uninitialised-memory bug with a one-line fix; a
           reproducer is `mount -t binfs /bin; ls -l /bin` on any config with
           BUILTIN + FS_BINFS (e.g. sim:nsh). Check master first: binfs_stat
           may have been fixed there already.

Apply: git -C ../nuttx apply ../vaporOS/patches/nuttx/vfs-stat-zero-mountpoint.patch   (setup.sh does this)

diff --git a/fs/vfs/fs_stat.c b/fs/vfs/fs_stat.c
index 7e4a29ac79..cec4bf0e1b 100644
--- a/fs/vfs/fs_stat.c
+++ b/fs/vfs/fs_stat.c
@@ -118,8 +118,12 @@ static int stat_recursive(FAR const char *path,
 
       if (inode->u.i_mops && inode->u.i_mops->stat)
         {
-          /* Perform the stat() operation */
+          /* Perform the stat() operation.  Many filesystems fill in only
+           * the fields they know about (binfs sets just the mode and size),
+           * so start from zeros as the pseudo-filesystem path below does.
+           */
 
+          RESET_BUF(buf);
           ret = inode->u.i_mops->stat(inode, desc.relpath, buf);
         }
       else
